    "updated_at": "2024-10-09T09:51:38Z",
    "body": "@karlt is correct.\r\n\r\nAn `error` attribute on `HTMLSourceElement` would be more consistent. Though `source` is also used for `img` where this kind of information is not exposed (and the `error` event is always fired on the `img` element), but it seems OK to leave `error` as null for images.",
